In the early game, I find a difficult balance between starving vs.
fighting vs. healing.  It goes something like this:

A. I need food, I'll go kill something and eat it.

B. Whew, no longer hungry, but now I need to heal hit points.  I'll
rest/try to avoid combat.

C. Uh-oh, hungry again, better go do some more killing, even though my
hit points haven't quite healed up...

Lather, rinse, repeat, get a free comprehensive inventory
identification.

So is this (a) something I'm not quite getting, or (b) the fundamental
tension/challenge in the game.  Food really seems a lot bigger deal in
NetHack than in the *bands.

I don't really have a problem finding food (I have only needed to pray
for food once), but seem to always be on a food = fighting = lower hit
points = trend towards death cycle.

Or is it the case that I'm not descending fast enough?  I try to see
most of a level before dropping down.  Do things get easier once you
get to levels that have more stores?  Or am I fundamentally missing
something about how to heal up hit points?

Oddly, I've found the healer and monk to be the easiest starting
classes (in terms of surviving the longest under my inexperienced
direction), which is contrary to the usual "start with a valkryie"
advice.  The healer starts with abundant healing; the monk with
abundant food.



